OCI DATABASE START:

ps -ef | grep d.bin

cd /u01/app/19.0.0.0/grid/bin

./crsctl start crs -wait

./crsctl check crs

 and start in OCI Replication:

connect user oracle:
sudo su - oracle

now check listner is up or not:
lsnrctl status

after check listner up now start database as mount:
startup mount;

after that start MRP:
ALTER DATABASE RECOVER MANAGED STANDBY DATABASE USING CURRENT LOGFILE DISCONNECT FROM SESSION;

Now check status of LOGs:
select process, status, sequence# from v$managed_standby;

it show applying log means MRP start properly.


